  "body": "## What changed\n\nFirst slice of #1442: lathe chucks generated as built-in fixture accessories.\n\n- `camcraft_sim::chuck` (new): `JawChuck` (body diameter/length, through bore, grip diameter, jaw length/width/height) and `ColletChuck` (body, nose diameter/length, collet bore). Each builds closed steel shells (body annulus + 2..12 jaws, or nose over body) and validates its figures by name: non-finite, zero, negative or absurd sizes, a bore past the body, jaws reaching past the body or meeting each other, a collet bore past the nose, a nose wider than the body.\n- `app::accessory`: three new kinds `three_jaw_chuck`, `four_jaw_chuck`, `collet_chuck` (\"3-jaw chuck\", \"4-jaw chuck\", \"Collet chuck\") with generic default figures; placed by the undoable `InsertAccessory`, resized by `SetAccessory`, one undo each.\n- New placement `AccessoryPlacement::OnStock` (`accessory::chuck::fit_to_stock`): closes the chuck on the setup's round stock on its axis (jaw face at the stock's underside; a collet the nose length deeper). Square stock, no stock, or a non-chuck kind is refused by name.\n- MCP `add_accessory`: the chuck kinds, their dimensions in the schema, and a `fit_to_stock` flag.\n- The UI dialog lists the new kinds through `accessory::KINDS` and places them by pose (no UI code change).\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/1442-lathe-chuck-fixtures.md` (frame, conservative facetting, no mill refusal, chucks not `fixed`).\n\n## How tested\n\n- `camcraft-sim` `tests/lathe_chuck.rs`: `three_jaw_envelope_is_pinned`, `four_jaw_has_four_jaws_at_quarters`, `collet_envelope_is_pinned` (body diameter and length, jaw reach and height, nose, bore - by bounds and point containment), `jaw_chuck_nonsense_is_refused_by_name`, `collet_nonsense_is_refused_by_name`, `round_stock_fits_and_square_stock_is_refused`.\n- `camcraft-app` `tests/lathe_chuck.rs`: `a_generated_chuck_is_steel_the_holder_law_reads` (an offset holder in the jaws is named and blocks the post), `the_same_holder_above_the_jaws_posts`, `a_chuck_fits_on_round_stock_and_refuses_by_name`.\n- `tests/mcp_accessory.rs`: `lathe_chucks_are_placed_fitted_to_the_stock_and_undone_over_mcp`; `tests/builtin_accessory.rs` updated for the nine kinds.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green (sim suites 18 s, app suites 45 s). Clippy `-p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings`: clean. UI `fixture_accessory` lib tests: 6 passed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The chucks' look in the viewport and the dialog in the running app were not seen; a screenshot is owed by the maintainer.\n- No \"Fit to the stock\" toggle in the UI dialog yet; inside grip, stepped jaws, independent 4-jaw offsets, rpm limit, 4th-axis chuck on a mill, camcraft-mcp skill row: filed as #1468.\n- Release lanes and pixel snapshots were not run.\n\nChangelog: Fixtures can generate 3-jaw, 4-jaw and collet lathe chucks as collision steel, fitted to round stock over MCP (#1442)\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #1442\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
